      "content": "The Caucasus region is a complex and volatile area, and any attempt to navigate its politics is fraught with risk. In the South Caucasus, the most stable and moderate governments are in Azerbaijan, under Ilham Aliyev, and Georgia, under Salome Zourabichvili, while Armenia's government, under Nikol Pashinyan, is seen as more progressive but still authoritarian. In the North Caucasus, the Russian government has a tight grip on the region, and any attempts to engage with local groups risk being seen as pro-Russian or pro-separatist.",
